<title>USA: Hallmark adopts shareholder rights plan.</title>
<headline>Hallmark adopts shareholder rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>WEST ALLIS, Wis. 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hallmark Capital Corp said on Tuesday it adopted a shareholder rights plan to held it fend off &quot;coercive, abusive or unfair takeover tactics.&quot;</p>
<p>Hallmark said the rights plan was not adopted in response to any specific offer or threat of a takeover.</p>
<p>The plan would give Hallmark shareholders a preferred stock purchase right, triggered when some person or group acquires at least 20 percent of Hallmark's common shares.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
